    description: "Adjacent finding of audit-findings 0021 (docs/audits/0021-logging-family.md, Step 5). Filed, not moved.\nipc_send is \"data sent to another process over a channel the program set up\" (the audit's definition, now in io_boundary_types and ADR-0050). These rows cross NO process boundary -- an in-process notification is delivered to observers in the same process:\n- objc NSNotificationCenter: postNotificationName:object:, postNotificationName:object:userInfo:, postNotification: (the row's own note: \"In-process pub/sub; classified as IPC for boundary analysis\")\n- swift NotificationCenter.post (\"In-process pub/sub notification posting\")\nTheir cross-process siblings NSDistributedNotificationCenter / DistributedNotificationCenter are correctly ipc_send and are NOT in scope.\nEffect: each post is an `ipc` taint sink and an ipc_send headline crossing. Not measured on a corpus.\nRelated: WI-rivur item 2 (NSNotificationCenter.removeObserver rowed ipc_recv) -- same root (\"a boundary chosen by what the call is ABOUT, not what it DOES\"), different rows.\nFix shape (not decided): delete the rows (no crossing), or a non-crossing representation if one exists. Measure the removal direction: every lost ipc finding must be read back."  # b5d1
    fields: {}  # b5d1
